<title>USA: Ralcorp insiders buy shares.</title>
<headline>Ralcorp insiders buy shares.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ralcorp Holdings Inc said Monday two company executives bought shares in the food company, which makes cereal, baby food, cookies and crackers.</p>
<p>Ralcorp Chairman William Stiritz bought 194,500 shares of company stock in three transactions between June 6 and June 11 at prices between $11.63 and $11.88 a share, Ralcorp spokesman Patrick Farrell said.</p>
<p>Stiritz now holds 858,126 shares of Ralcorp stock.</p>
<p>On June 6, Ralcorp Chief Executive Officer Joe Micheletto bought 17,000 shares at $12 a share, Farrell said. This brought Micheletto's holding to 42,090 Ralcorp shares.</p>
<p>Ralcorp shares were up 1-1/8 at 17-1/4 on Monday afternoon.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
